#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# weierstrass_e1

#% text
# `weierstrass_e1([g2, g3])` gives the root `e1 = weierstrass_p(omega1, [g2, g3])` of `4 t^3 - g2 t - g3`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The half-periods `omega_k` are those of `weierstrass_half_periods` (`omega2 = -omega1 - omega3`).

#% item
# The three roots add up to zero; for `[a, 0]` with `a > 0` and `[0, b]` with `b > 0` the values are closed forms.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
weierstrass_e1([11.0, 7.0])
#% output
#= 1.9142135623730951

#% cell
n(weierstrass_e1([5, 1]), 25)
#% output
#= 1.2071067811865475244008443621

#% cell
weierstrass_e1([0.5 + im, 1.0])
#% output
#= -0.4629125711663471 - 0.5567903033680378im

#% cell
weierstrass_e1([1, 0])
#% output
#= 1/2

#% text
# The roots add up to zero:

#% cell
weierstrass_e1([5.0, 1.0]) + weierstrass_e2([5.0, 1.0]) + weierstrass_e3([5.0, 1.0])
#% output
#= 0.0

